---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';

const runtimeValue = (name: string, buildValue?: string) =>
  buildValue?.trim() || `[[RENART env \`${name}\` | html RENART]]`;

const legalName = runtimeValue('RENART_LEGAL_NAME', import.meta.env.PUBLIC_RENART_LEGAL_NAME);
const addressLine = runtimeValue(
  'RENART_LEGAL_ADDRESS_LINE_1',
  import.meta.env.PUBLIC_RENART_LEGAL_ADDRESS_LINE_1,
);
const postalCode = runtimeValue(
  'RENART_LEGAL_POSTAL_CODE',
  import.meta.env.PUBLIC_RENART_LEGAL_POSTAL_CODE,
);
const city = runtimeValue('RENART_LEGAL_CITY', import.meta.env.PUBLIC_RENART_LEGAL_CITY);
const country = runtimeValue(
  'RENART_LEGAL_COUNTRY',
  import.meta.env.PUBLIC_RENART_LEGAL_COUNTRY,
);
const email = runtimeValue('RENART_LEGAL_EMAIL', import.meta.env.PUBLIC_RENART_LEGAL_EMAIL);
const analyticsRetentionDays = runtimeValue(
  'RENART_ANALYTICS_RETENTION_DAYS',
  import.meta.env.PUBLIC_RENART_ANALYTICS_RETENTION_DAYS,
);
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="How getrenart.com processes personal data and which choices you have."
  alternateHref="/datenschutz/"
>
  <p>
    <strong>Translation notice:</strong> This English version is provided for convenience. In
    the event of discrepancies, the <a href="/datenschutz/" hreflang="de">German version</a>
    applies.
  </p>
  <p><strong>Last updated: 12 August 2026</strong></p>

  <h2>1. Controller</h2>
  <address>
    <strong>{legalName}</strong><br />
    {addressLine}<br />
    {postalCode} {city}<br />
    {country}<br />
    Email: {email}
  </address>

  <h2>2. Delivery and protection of the website</h2>
  <p>
    This website is hosted on a server operated by netcup GmbH, Emmy-Noether-Straße 10,
    76131 Karlsruhe, Germany. We have concluded a data processing agreement with netcup
    pursuant to Article 28 GDPR. The web server operated by Renart does not keep its own
    access log.
  </p>
  <p>
    Cloudflare, Inc., 101 Townsend St, San Francisco, CA 94107, USA, provides DNS, reverse
    proxy, security, and content delivery functions. Requests to this website therefore pass
    through the Cloudflare network first. In particular, Cloudflare may process the IP
    address, time, requested address, HTTP and device information, and data used to detect
    and prevent abusive access. Cloudflare may also process data outside the EU or EEA; the
    agreed data protection safeguards, including the EU Standard Contractual Clauses, apply
    to such processing.
  </p>
  <p>
    This processing is necessary to deliver the expressly requested website securely,
    reliably, and quickly. The legal basis is Article 6(1)(f) GDPR. Our legitimate interest
    is the secure and uninterrupted operation of the website. Technical data is processed
    only for as long as necessary for delivery, troubleshooting, abuse prevention, or legal
    obligations.
  </p>
  <p>
    Further information is available in the privacy notices of{' '}
    <a href="https://www.netcup.com/de/kontakt/datenschutzerklaerung">netcup</a> and{' '}
    <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Storage of your privacy and interface choices</h2>
  <p>
    The consent manager stores the technically necessary cookie <code>renart_consent</code>{' '}
    after you make a privacy choice. It contains your accepted categories, consent version,
    language, a randomly generated consent identifier, and the timestamps of your first and
    latest choice. The cookie is sent with requests to getrenart.com but is not evaluated by
    the web server. It expires after 180 days unless you change your choice or delete it
    earlier. This prevents the banner from returning on every page visit and lets us respect
    your decision. You can change it at any time through <strong>Privacy settings</strong> in
    the footer. The legal basis is section 25(2)(2) TDDDG and, to the extent that personal
    data is processed, Article 6(1)(f) GDPR.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you dismiss the Discord invitation, we also store only the value <code>1</code> under
    the key <code>renart.discord-invite-dismissed.v1</code> in your browser's local storage.
    This prevents a dismissed invitation from appearing again on subsequent pages. This
    preference is likewise not transmitted to our server and can be reset by clearing your
    browser's local storage. The legal basis is section 25(2)(2) TDDDG and, to the extent
    that personal data is processed, Article 6(1)(f) GDPR.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Optional audience measurement</h2>
  <p>
    Only if you expressly consent does this website activate our self-hosted, cookie-free
    audience measurement. We operate it on infrastructure in Germany; the data is not
    disclosed to a separate analytics provider. Before you consent, no analytics code is
    loaded and no analytics event is sent.
  </p>
  <p>
    When audience measurement is enabled, we process the page path and title, referrer,
    hostname, screen resolution, and browser language. Search parameters and URL fragments
    are excluded. Technically transmitted information, including the IP address and user
    agent, is used to generate a rotating session identifier; the raw IP address is not
    stored as an analytics value. This produces statistics about page views, sessions,
    countries of origin, browsers, operating systems, and device types. We do not use the
    analytics service to identify people or track them across other websites, and it does
    not set analytics cookies. We also respect an enabled Do Not Track preference in your
    browser.
  </p>
  <p>
    The legal bases are your consent under section 25(1) TDDDG and Article 6(1)(a) GDPR.
    Analytics events are deleted after no more than{' '}
    <strong>{analyticsRetentionDays} days</strong>. You can withdraw your consent at any time
    with future effect through <strong>Privacy settings</strong> in the page footer. The
    lawfulness of processing before withdrawal remains unaffected.
  </p>

  <h2>5. External links and the Discord community</h2>
  <p>
    Links to GitHub and Discord are ordinary links. We do not embed content from these
    providers; a connection is established only when you open a link.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you join the Renart community on Discord, Discord processes your account, usage, and
    communication data under its own responsibility. For people in the EEA, Discord names
    Discord Netherlands B.V. as the controller. Server administrators can see your public
    profile name, roles, contributions, and necessary moderation actions. We use only
    Discord's built-in AutoMod feature and no additional bots or separate bot logs. Our
    processing serves to operate and protect the voluntarily used community on the basis of
    Article 6(1)(b) and (f) GDPR. Our legitimate interest is a helpful and safe project
    community. Discord may process data in third countries, particularly the USA. Details
    and deletion options are described in{' '}
    <a href="https://discord.com/privacy">Discord's privacy policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Contacting us</h2>
  <p>
    If you contact us by email, we process your sender address, the content of your message,
    and any accompanying data required to respond. The legal basis is Article 6(1)(b) GDPR
    where the request concerns pre-contractual or contractual matters, and otherwise Article
    6(1)(f) GDPR. We delete correspondence once the request has been conclusively resolved,
    unless statutory retention or evidence obligations require otherwise.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
  <p>Subject to the statutory conditions, you have in particular the right to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>access personal data processed about you (Article 15 GDPR),</li>
    <li>rectification of inaccurate data (Article 16 GDPR),</li>
    <li>erasure or restriction of processing (Articles 17 and 18 GDPR),</li>
    <li>data portability (Article 20 GDPR),</li>
    <li>object to processing under Article 6(1)(f) GDPR (Article 21 GDPR),</li>
    <li>withdraw consent with future effect (Article 7(3) GDPR).</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    You also have the right to lodge a complaint with a data protection supervisory
    authority, particularly in the place of your habitual residence, your place of work, or
    the place of the alleged infringement. To exercise your rights, send a message to the
    email address stated above.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Automated decisions</h2>
  <p>
    We do not make decisions based solely on automated processing, including profiling,
    within the meaning of Article 22 GDPR.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
